  "review_text": "This month featured seven graded stories, spread over six issues (<i>Strange Tales</i> with two, as always), yielding a final weighted average of [SPAN: severity=info; fontsize=large; fonttype=bold; text=x.xx],\n\n... last month's <b>5.74</b>.\n\n\nThis may seem surprising given the high-quality of both the <i>Journey Into Mystery</i> and <i>Amazing Spider-Man</i> offerings, but unfortunately they were paired with the equally-horrible <i>Tales to Astonish</i> and <i>Fantastic Four</i>.&nbsp; It was a very uneven month with great variation.\n\nHighlights of the month were the surprisingly good Thor and Spider-Man stories, neither of which featured main-line villains, so the plots on these and the characterization won the day.&nbsp; However, the Porcupine, Infant Terrible, and the Scarecrow were all lame as all get-out and really dragged the rest of them down!&nbsp; The Wizard's appearance didn't help matters either, though we finally saw a glimmer of hope for Dr. Strange at least.\n\n\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** SUMMARY_BEGIN ***\n*** THIS MONTH ***0 graded stories over 0 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 0 grade character issue weight0.00*** LAST MONTH ***9 graded stories over 8 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 6.83 grade character issue    weight 9.2   asm       ASM #9   1.00 6.5   xmen      XMEN #3  1.00 6.0   ff        FF #23   1.00 6.0   iron      TOS #50  0.50 5.5   aven      AVEN #3  1.25 5.5   thor      JIM #100 0.50 4.5   giant     TTA #52  0.75 1.8   torch     ST #117  0.50 1.8   strange   ST #117  0.335.74\n*** SUMMARY_END ***]",
  "letters_page": "[DEVNOTE: *** INTRODUCTION_BEGIN ***\n*** INTRODUCTION_END ***]\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_BEGIN ***]\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_END ***]",
  "ownership": "That brings us to the end of 1963, but looking ahead to next month, the Avengers welcome the return of another Golden Age hero from the 1940s, Magneto rolls out the debut of a new \"brotherhood,\" Doc Ock makes a return, the Black Widow debuts, and the Thing takes on the Hulk!"
